# Data representation conversion keeps the unit

Verifies `->to(type)` changes only the numeric representation of a data measure while preserving its unit. An integer byte becomes a decimal byte, a float kilobyte becomes a decimal kilobyte, and a whole decimal byte becomes an integer byte. Each assignment to an explicitly typed variable proves the representation changed, since a mismatched base type would fail compilation.

>>> source
whole: int = 1B
as_decimal: decimal = whole->to(decimal)
print(as_decimal)
float_val: float = 1.5KB
float_as_decimal: decimal = float_val->to(decimal)
print(float_as_decimal)
whole_decimal: decimal = 2B
back_to_int: int = whole_decimal->to(int)
print(back_to_int)

<<< stdout
1B
1.5KB
2B

<<< stderr
